# The step of the map mul_pow2_map_2, an array of two limbs times a power of two: mul_pow2_2. The
# program supplies both; mul_pow2_2 only multiplies them, so rule R3 asks no guard. Its claims
# are those of mul_pow2_2.
kernel:        mul_pow2_step_2
input:         supplied x = x0 x1
input:         c
output:        z = z0 z1
value:         x*c
requires:      normalized x
requires:      power_of_two c
ensures:       normalized z
ensures:       error z R c=0 k=2 t=1
min_precision: 2
theorem:       proofs/theories/MapSteps.v mul_pow2_step_2_correct
source:        mul_pow2_2, the two limbs scaled and renormalized
license:       algorithm: published; proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes

(z0, z1) = mul_pow2_2(x0, x1, c)
